{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime\/init(tt:)"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"init","externalID":"s:12AstronomyKit9AstroTimeV2ttACSd_tcfc","title":"init(tt:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"tt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astrotime\/init(tt:)"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a time from Terrestrial Time days since J2000."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tt"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"tt","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Terrestrial Time days since noon on January 1, 2000.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Terrestrial Time is used for calculations not involving Earth’s rotation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(planetary orbits, eclipses, etc.). This initializer is the inverse of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime\/init(ut:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — it starts from a TT value and derives the corresponding UT."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If TT falls in a positive discontinuity gap in the selected Delta T model,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UT clamps to the first representable coordinate after the jump while TT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"remains unchanged. At a negative jump with two solutions, fixed-point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iteration returns the first solution reached from its initial "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ut = tt"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"estimate. Because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" stores UT, encoding a gap-clamped value and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decoding it derives TT again from the selected model."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nonfinite or nonconvergent input produces an invalid time with NaN fields."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstroTime/init(tt:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astrotime\/init(tt:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"tt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime\/init(tt:)","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a time from Terrestrial Time days since J2000.","type":"text"}],"title":"init(tt:)"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit","title":"AstronomyKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift bindings for Don Cross’ "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" library."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstroTime":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime","kind":"symbol","title":"AstroTime","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represents a moment in time for astronomical calculations."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AstroTime","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AstroTime","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astrotime"},"https://github.com/cosinekitty/astronomy":{"title":"Astronomy Engine","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Astronomy Engine"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","type":"link"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstroTime/init(ut:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astrotime\/init(ut:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime\/init(ut:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a time from modeled UT1 days since J2000."}],"title":"init(ut:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ut"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]}}}